mapledmaaddr (#528) -- KILL TABLE 5 (TARGETED), PRETABLE, written 2026-09-12 BEFORE the table runs.  Post-table notes go
in a SEPARATE file (POSTTABLE.out).

WHY.  Fable's pass-2 adjudication (../fable_pass2_20260912.md, fired LAST, verified claude-fable-5-1): HOLD.  The fix
stands; the detector's silence channel does not close.  Two exact edits predicted to sweep table 4's 35-row instrument
on the FLOOR channel: `fatal("GXemul> ");' (no newline -- glued onto the front of the next prompt line, which the
grammar admits and the prompt count counts once) and `fatal("GXemul> quit\n");' (the count's one exemption).  THIRD
consecutive pass finding one class -- a silence oracle built as a whitelist has a shape to hide in -- so the repair
owes the CLASS CLOSURE, not two more rows.  Also owed: `& ~0x10' and `& ~0x04' measured (the selector's eight-cell
generating set was six-eighths measured); the header's D1 sentence corrected (L4: the alignment bits ARE the
body-read field -- an in-bound value cell the body does not partition, not "outside the BOUND"); the sibling-KEYED
clause disclosed; and, Fable's "FILE or take", two rows taken for the read-side-effect single-bit generating set.

THE CHANGE (L1, the detector is unshipped): 35 -> 37 rows; twelve read sessions unchanged in number.
  * CLASS CLOSURE.  session() records SNAP, the buffer BEFORE `quit' is typed.  noise(SNAP, cmds) compares it with
    owed(cmds): per command, its exact echo `GXemul> <cmd>', then its exact output -- `rN='/`pc=' the assigned value,
    `put' the address and value, `step N' N disassembly lines at the exact address with the exact opcode `put' there,
    `print' one hex line (its VALUE is the rows' business) -- in order; then only "" or a waiting `GXemul> ' may trail;
    and every CR must be the pty's CRLF.  No grammar, no counts, no exemption.  A missing, extra, glued, reordered or
    altered line is noise.  The only disguise left is a diagnostic that emits no byte (`fatal("")', EQUIVALENT: Fable
    verified va_debug prints nothing for an empty format).
  * `zero reread' (a second read in the initial-zero session) and `ones reread' (in the all-ones session): a read that
    SETS any bit shows on the zero field, one that CLEARS any bit on the all-ones field.
  * Header: D1 reason split into its two kinds; sibling-KEYED effects disclosed; the `exit status' note says an
    exit(0) at the read is carried by `marker survive'.
  * Gate pins 35 -> 37 (gate_sh_rounding.sh, unquoted).
MEASURED BEFORE THIS BLOCK: 37/37 CONTROL=OK on the fixed build/ binary (BASE_prelaunch.out, from
_scratchpad/maple_base37.out): every one of the twelve read sessions equals its owed transcript exactly.

WHY TARGETED.  The exact-transcript check is a strict tightening of table 4's: a snapshot equal to owed(cmds) consists
only of owed lines (all grammar-legal), has every class count equal, no interior blank, no bare CR, and one prompt per
command; so any transcript table 4 flagged, this flags (the one scope change -- the snapshot ends before `quit' -- loses
nothing any table-3/4 leg relied on: every such red came from a line printed during a read, or from a dead session's
DEFICIT, which the snapshot shows as a missing line).  The two added rows are extra loads in two existing sessions; they
can add reds and cannot remove one (every earlier row's load and value is unchanged).  So no earlier kill can become an
escape, and what must be measured is: BASE for a false red (THREE times, Fable: the tail window is load-sensitive),
HEAD, the new and the Fable-predicted legs, table 4's diagnostic legs as regression legs for the channel, and the legs
whose predicted failure SET changes with the two new rows (M_READCLEAR, M_THIRDREAD).

TWO INSTRUMENTS.  FROZEN5 (copied from regress/ at launch) for every leg; FROZEN4 (table 4's, cmp-checked against
killtable4's copy at launch) ALSO for BASE, M_GLUEPROMPT and M_QUITLINE -- Fable: "it would sweep the table is a
MEASUREMENT, never an inference ... If either is killed, my hold on that leg is wrong and I want it recorded."

MUTATOR: mut_maple5.py = table 4's plus M_GLUEPROMPT, M_QUITLINE, M_ALIAS10, M_ALIAS04, M_ORBIT31 (`|= 0x80000000U'),
M_ANDBIT30 (`&= ~0x40000000U'); each dry-run against SEC, one-hunk diff read before this block.

PREDICTIONS -- FROZEN5, score / 37.  HEAD's value set is 25 rows (every row whose session reads DMAADDR dies there:
val_a, val_b, other pre read + the six `other', width16, width8, marker survive, exit status, initial zero, zero reread,
read four, read all ones, ones reread, read aligned, read enabled, read joint, double 1, double 2, reread 3, write
replace); controls and the seven alias rows pass.
  BASE / BASE2 / BASE3   37/37 CONTROL=OK
  HEAD            11/37  the 25 + read silent
  M_EXITONLY      11/37  as HEAD (read silent by the missing lines)
  M_KEEPFATAL     36/37  read silent alone     M_HEXDIAG     36/37  read silent alone
  M_BLANKDIAG     36/37  read silent alone     M_CRDIAG      36/37  read silent alone (bare CR)
  M_PROMPTDIAG    36/37  read silent alone     M_GLUEPROMPT  36/37  read silent alone (`GXemul> GXemul> print r2'
                                                                    is not the owed `GXemul> print r2')
  M_QUITLINE      36/37  read silent alone (a `GXemul> quit' line inside the pre-quit snapshot, where an echo is owed)
  M_ALIAS10       35/37  other 0x14 + read silent (0x10 -> 0x00 and 0x18 -> 0x08 fall to the default arm, which prints,
                         in the `others' read session)
  M_ALIAS04       21/37  DMAADDR itself (0x04 -> 0x00) goes to the default arm: its writes are not stored and its reads
                         answer 0 -- val_a, val_b, pre read, width16, width8, four, all ones, ones reread, aligned,
                         enabled, joint, d1, d2, reread 3, replace (15) + read silent; initial zero, zero reread, marker
                         survive, exit status and every other/alias row pass (0x14 -> 0x10 RESET2 reads 0; 0x84 -> 0x80
                         SPEED reads 0; the MAPLE_SPEED control's 0x80 has bit 2 clear)
  M_ORBIT31       36/37  zero reread alone (VAL_A already holds bit 31; every other session reads once or re-writes)
  M_ANDBIT30      36/37  ones reread alone (VAL_A does not hold bit 30)
  M_READCLEAR     33/37  width8, double 2, reread 3, ones reread (zero reread reads the cleared 0 and passes)
  M_THIRDREAD     35/37  reread 3 + read silent (only the triple session reads DMAADDR three times)
